WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.604
Some machines have a program
deciding what they do.

2
00:00:07.824 --> 00:00:12.515
Some things talk to the internet,
and robots build cars in factories.

3
00:00:13.015 --> 00:00:20.259
A program controls a machine when a small computer
inside decides what it does: it is computer-controlled.

4
00:00:20.479 --> 00:00:26.749
A washing machine runs a program: it
decides when to turn, heat and stop.

5
00:00:26.969 --> 00:00:32.217
Traffic lights and a lift have programs
too. An automatic door opens for a sensor.

6
00:00:32.437 --> 00:00:36.802
A bicycle, a whisk and a broom have
no program. You do all the work.

7
00:00:37.022 --> 00:00:40.412
So ask: is a computer
deciding, or are you?

8
00:00:40.912 --> 00:00:44.070
A bulb, a doorbell, a thermostat, a plug.

9
00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:47.773
Add a small computer inside,
connected to the internet.

10
00:00:47.993 --> 00:00:52.219
That is an Internet of Things
device: a smart device.

11
00:00:52.439 --> 00:00:55.922
Smart does not mean
clever. It means connected.

12
00:00:56.142 --> 00:00:59.811
A smart watch counts your steps
and sends them to your phone.

13
00:01:00.031 --> 00:01:04.071
A smart bulb switches on from your
phone, even from another town.

14
00:01:04.291 --> 00:01:07.356
The lamp beside it, with
a switch, is not smart.

15
00:01:07.856 --> 00:01:11.246
Robots weld the car's
metal body, then paint it.

16
00:01:11.466 --> 00:01:15.228
A robot lifts the engine in, then
fits the doors and the wheels.

17
00:01:15.448 --> 00:01:17.445
People test the finished car.

18
00:01:17.665 --> 00:01:20.590
Six steps, most of them done by a robot.

19
00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:25.734
Exact. A robot welds in the same
place, to the millimetre, every time.

20
00:01:25.954 --> 00:01:30.923
Heavy. An engine is too heavy to
lift. A robot arm lifts it in.

21
00:01:31.143 --> 00:01:35.695
Dangerous. Paint fumes and hot
metal are safer for a robot.

22
00:01:35.915 --> 00:01:41.998
Repeated: the same repetitive step, ten
thousand times a day, and it never gets tired.

23
00:01:42.218 --> 00:01:47.466
And the people: they program each robot,
check every car, and fix what breaks.

24
00:01:47.686 --> 00:01:53.026
Robots did not take all the jobs. They
do the steps; people run the factory.

25
00:01:53.526 --> 00:01:57.567
The program decides: move
here, weld, move back.

26
00:01:57.787 --> 00:02:01.781
The motors are outputs. They move
the arm where the program says.

27
00:02:02.001 --> 00:02:05.855
The sensors are inputs. They tell
the program where the arm is.

28
00:02:06.075 --> 00:02:10.858
The stop button is an input too.
Press it, and every motor stops.

29
00:02:11.078 --> 00:02:16.419
A factory robot is a computer controlling
a machine, just like the automatic door.

30
00:02:16.919 --> 00:02:20.448
A program can control a
machine, deciding what it does.

31
00:02:20.668 --> 00:02:25.127
Everyday things that connect to the
internet are the Internet of Things.

32
00:02:25.347 --> 00:02:30.223
Robots do the exact, heavy, dangerous
and repeated jobs in a factory.

33
00:02:30.443 --> 00:02:35.505
And a robot is a computer controlling
a machine: sensors in, motors out.
